A||||2||Fformula88||Fiero rebuilding about to begin after accident.||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||01-20-2001||10:49 PM||||If anyone didn't see my previous posts, last weekend a car spun out in front of me while I was driving my dads 87 coupe.  I hit him doing going fairly fast in his passenger doors (maybe about 40).  The Fiero faired fairly well, but there is damage to the front impact bar, hood and headlight assemblies.  There is also some damage to the passenger side from an accident last year.<P>This week we looked at a couple Fiero's for sale locally, including a sweet 84 SE with a Kamei (?) body kit.  Well, its way to much $$ and not really worth it.  So Yesterday started disassembling the 87 to see what exactly was left.<P>Much to my surprise, the main frame rails are in good shape!  There is a little damage, but today we pounded the stuff back into decent shape.  The front impact bar, however, is kinda mangled and shot.<P>Well, after searching a couple junk yards to see if we could come up with parts, we found an 87 coupe with a blown engine, but nearly all of its body intact!  This is a great find since we need both front fenders, the front fascia, hood, pass. side quarter panel and rear fascia.  It also has both headlight assemblies intact with motors.  So Monday we are going back to strip it.<P>Instead of junking another Fiero, we are rebuilding it!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I am so pleased we won't have to get rid of the Fiero!  Its in very rough shape anyway, so this will get it a bunch of good body panels and a new paint job!  Its just such a good feeling knowing we can save the car and don't have to junk her.  It would be a shame after 130K miles!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
